     "content": "# Gauge-invariant branch reconstruction and robust discrimination v0.1\n\nDERIVED CONDITIONAL mathematics on the frozen 15-node, 28-link, 18-diamond action. Development lane; independent review PENDING; physical promotion 0. No registry entry.\n\nFor a diamond based at k, define z_d=-psi_k^dagger W_d psi_k/(psi_k^dagger psi_k). This complex scalar is invariant under the full local U(r) gauge group and common matter phase. On the one-active-color embeddings, z_d=exp(i(C theta)_d). In the local phase chart, phi=Arg z=C theta.\n\nWith L=CZ and L^T L=Gamma I, the critical coordinate is EXACTLY b=L^T phi/Gamma on the Lyapunov-Schmidt sheet theta=Zb+y, Z^T D y=0. This holds at every finite rank for these embeddings; it does not classify arbitrary color-normal configurations.\n\nP4=sum b_j^4/(sum b_j^2)^2 equals 1, 1/2, 1/3 on the six balanced, twelve index-one and eight index-two branches. The signed cubic C3=3 sqrt(3) b1 b2 b3/||b||^3 is zero for the first two and +/-1 for the last. Full labeled b distinguishes 26 branches. Real loop and density channels are exactly blind to the opposite overall phase. Six labeled real vertex-loop channels recover squared pair distances in the critical truncation and yield asymptotic class fingerprints 1/4, 1/2, 7/12 on the full branches.\n\nIf the oriented phase error is bounded in Euclidean norm by delta, then e=delta/sqrt(Gamma) bounds critical-coordinate error. e<=||b||/7 guarantees nearest-P4-class discrimination; a directly usable sufficient guard is 8e<=||b_hat||. The proved fingerprint error is <=97/1296<1/12. This bound presumes the local embedded branch model and includes no unbounded systematic error.\n\nFor the stable family, omega_radial^2/omega_angular^2 tends to 1+4 A4/B4=4.746844460896146...; the frequency ratio tends to 2.1787254211800406.... The limit is independent of common clock scaling, N and the critical mass. It is an asymptotic model-conditional prediction, not a new empirical result.\n\n64 exact