+# Certified finite-offset region and errors
+
+Conditional on the unchanged frozen action, 0 < epsilon <= 1/100000 is certified for all 26 labeled phase branches. A 44-variable analytic rescaling removes the threshold singularity. Three global solution boxes and 1536 nested parameter boxes establish the continuation and scalar indices 0, 1 and 2. The six balanced branches are scalar orbital minima; saddle embeddings remain unstable through their invariant scalar subsystem. Full-rank finite-offset stability of the minima is not certified here.
+
+With R the critical readout radius, q_k=A4+3B4/4-B4/(2k), the amplitude error satisfies |R^2/(Gamma*epsilon/(4*q_k))-1|<=25*epsilon. Fast-loop error is <=297*epsilon^(3/2). The six-real-loop fingerprint bias is <=41*epsilon relative to {1/4,1/2,7/12}. On this interval 2*sqrt(epsilon)<R<(5/2)*sqrt(epsilon), matter components exceed 1/5, the hopping ground gap exceeds 3/5 and all diamond phases are smaller than 1/16 radian.
+
+Sufficient calibrated deterministic readout budgets: oriented phase L2 error <=5*sqrt(epsilon), or six labeled real-channel errors each <=epsilon/40. Both guarantee classification; real-only readout still loses the overall phase sign.
+
+For a=N=r=1, 2048 rigorous symmetry-sector spectral cut tests prove 14.17<omega_radial^2/epsilon<14.20 and 2.98<omega_angular^2/epsilon<2.998. Thus 7085/1499<omega_radial^2/omega_angular^2<710/149 and the frequency ratio differs from sqrt(1+4*A4/B4) by less than 1/200. This is a finite-offset bound, not an unnormalized physical frequency prediction.
+
+Computer-assisted constructor certification; independent review PENDING; development, no registry entry; physical promotion 0. No maximality or exhaustive finite-offset classification outside the certified tubes. No empirical reanalysis.
